  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Border of Water and Ice (2024), published by Cornell University Press, has been cited 2 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 674 times and is used in teaching.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Border of Water and Ice by Joseph A. Seeley was published by Cornell University Press in 2024. Conceptually, the work connects to Geology and Geography. The book was recognised: ACLS Open Access Book Prize & Arcadia Open Access Publishing Award finalist (2026) \u2014 History.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 2 citations. Citations peaked in 2025 with 1 citing works. Notable citing venues include Oxford Research Encyclopedia of Asian History and Environmental History. The citing authors are based in the United States.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In teaching, it is discussed in 2 recorded lectures. It has been downloaded 674 times via OAPEN and Ubiquity Press.</p>",
